  "notes": "Piano solo on ONE grand staff (brace). A correct conversion yields exactly ONE part \"Piano\" with 2 staves; it must NOT be split into right/left hand parts, and the second right-hand voice in bars 13-16 must stay inside the piano part (voice 2), not become a new part. DAMAGE (yellowed): Aged paper in an RGB scan: cream to brown paper, brown faded ink with uneven density, age darkening at the edges, paper fibres, foxing spots (scan 40, severe 150 spots up to 3.5 mm, which can resemble dots/staccato marks). Severe adds faint bleed-through and blur. TRUTH LIMITATIONS: Foxing spots are random brown dots, not music; some can sit on staff lines and look like staccato dots or tiny noteheads. Truth contains none of them."
